// === PREAMBLE ===
// @trope    Fire-Forged Friends
// @category Friendship
// @source   https://allthetropes.org/wiki/Fire-Forged_Friends
// @domain   Narrative
// @version  1.3
//
// Laconic (per the wiki): characters who were hostile, indifferent, or strangers are forced to fight on
// the same side — and come out of it friends. FRONTIER: the bond forged BY shared battle. The
// discriminator is a [+Wary] character (one who began at a guarded distance) bound on the agent of a
// [&FightsBeside] event with another — so it fires when fighting shoulder to shoulder turns wariness into
// a bond. Distinct from Defeat Means Friendship (one BESTS the other first) and Enemy Mine (a truce that
// stays hostile): here they fight TOGETHER and the wariness is spent into trust.


// === IMPORTS & ASSOCIATIONS ===
import "trl/concepts/index.trl"

assoc fire_forged_friends -> [
  defeat_means_friendship : "the side-by-side counterpart to the beaten-then-joined",
  enemy_mine  : "the lasting bond a mere truce of",
  power_of_friendship : "the forged camaraderie that feeds"
]


// === ONTOLOGY ===
// — founded here (the guarded start spent into a battle-bond is the discriminator; reuses Bonded_To) —
prop Wary [+Psychological]   // holding another at a guarded distance — not (yet) a friend
verb FightsBeside(ally) [+Interpersonal] // fights shoulder to shoulder against a common foe

imply FireForgedFriends -> [Social, Narrative]


// === ABSTRACT RULE ===
// Naming rule: a [+Wary] character FIGHTS BESIDE another — the guarded one bound on the agent role of a
// [&FightsBeside] event (ally=$b), so phase-2 re-checks [+Wary] on the bound fighter (STYLE §8). Binding
// the guarded start on the one who fights alongside is the discriminator: the shared battle spends the
// wariness into a bond (the rule derives [@Bonded_To]), parting it from Defeat Means Friendship (a defeat
// precedes) and Enemy Mine (a truce that stays cold).
rule Fire_Forged_Friends {
  when:
    char $a [+Wary]
    char $b
    $a != $b
    evt  $battle [&FightsBeside(agent=$a, ally=$b)]
  then:
    $a [-Wary]
    $a [@Bonded_To(other=$b)]
    $battle [+FireForgedFriends]
}


// === CONCRETE VIGNETTE: Toy Story — Woody and Buzz (animated film, 1995) ===
// Woody and Buzz start as bitter rivals — Woody jealous of the flashy newcomer, Buzz dismissing the
// cowboy — and the rivalry strands them both in Sid's house, far from Andy. To get home they have no
// choice but to work as one: rigging the rescue, dodging the dog, and riding the rocket to catch the
// moving truck shoulder to shoulder. By the time they make it, the wariness is gone; the shared ordeal
// has forged them into best friends. Fire-forged.

// WOODY — guarded and jealous of the newcomer at the start
char woody [+Protagonist] [+Wary]

// BUZZ LIGHTYEAR — the rival he must fight alongside to get home
char buzz [+Deuteragonist]

scene the_escape_from_sids {
  beat 1 {
    // stranded together, they fight as one to get home — the forging
    evt the_rescue [&FightsBeside(agent=woody, ally=buzz)]
    // Fire_Forged_Friends -> woody [-Wary] [@Bonded_To(buzz)]; the_rescue [+FireForgedFriends]
  }
}
